.TH CHTTP_BASE64_DECODE 3 "2026-07-10" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Functions"
.SH NAME
chttp_base64_decode \- base64-decode a string (default allocator)
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <chttp.h>

void *chttp_base64_decode(const char *b64_input, size_t *out_len);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
Static inline wrapper around chttp_base64_decode_mp() with NULL
memory management procedures (uses malloc/free).
.fi
.SH PARAMETERS
.nf
b64_input  NUL-terminated base64 string to decode. Must not be NULL.
out_len    Optional; receives the decoded byte length. Pass NULL to
           ignore.
.fi
.SH RETURN VALUE
.nf
Newly allocated decoded buffer on success.
NULL on allocation failure or malformed input.
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR chttp_base64_decode_mp (3),
.BR chttp_base64_encode (3)
